+# estate_surge.dem — Story 5.12's named golden: a T2 frame of a CLUSTERED
+# topology under surge — drops at the shared uplink (the aggregation event,
+# spec-traffic-model Thread 3). A 3-campus ESTATE (the group-bias shape — the
+# campuses all sit within the group radius of a sibling, "homes grouped
+# together in estates") shares ONE player-built uplink: each campus rides fat
+# wide access drops (its OWN traffic never congests its drop — the 5.9 cap +
+# the 5.10 headroom) onto the estate router (R1), whose SHARED uplink to the
+# mesh (R0) is a 4-wide bundle that carries the BASE aggregate (3/tick = 90
+# u/s vs 160 u/s) and saturates under the ×10 surge (the capped 7.5/tick =
+# 225 u/s ask) — the honest aggregation choke. The eight residential sinks are
+# spread thin (delivery-side load per sink stays far under its drop), so the
+# shed stays AT THE SHARED UPLINK: the crisis engine names the uplink bundle,
+# the banner reads "Add a parallel pipe or a higher tier on the group
+# uplink's path — the surge is an aggregation event", and the player's fat
+# pipe (parallel wides) is the difference between base flowing and the surge
+# shedding. Captures: 25000ms (t500 — the clean estate BEFORE the surge, the
+# honest pre-crisis state) and 75000ms (t1500 — the surge active: drops at
+# the uplink + the crisis banner + the red bottleneck outline).
+#
+# T1 pins (replay gate + manifest): every per-tick hash, including the surge
+# window's aggregation drops (replay byte-identical [E10]).
